      "text": "Worker resolutions after the independent review (not a second independent review):\n\nblocker: physical WSS/VLESS dials now recover the establishment context explicitly,\nbind to tunnel lifetime, perform TLS under that budget, and register physical workers.\nTestTunnelPhysicalDialCancellationAndRestartWait verifies both protocols retain their\ndeadline, observe cancellation and prevent Restart returning before old work exits.\n\nblocker: VLESS bridge and packet/stream upload failures retain terminal classifications.\nTestVLESSIdentityFailuresSurviveBridgeAndRemainIsolated covers TCP and HTTP ingress,\ndownload and packet-upload 401/403, outer TLS rejection and successful TCP probes that\nmust not remove isolation.\n\nmajor: background probes use oldest-due ordering and refill freed concurrency immediately.\nTestBackgroundProbeRecoveryFairness runs 65 healthy endpoints plus an isolated endpoint\nunder a controlled clock, asserting recovery, healthy refresh, at most three in flight\nand no remaining work on close.\n\nmajor: H2 pool admission no longer closes an acquired connection. Overflow connections\nserve their assigned request without retention and close after use.\nTestHTTPSResponseMetadataAndPoolOverflow fills the pool and completes two real local\nrequests for both H1 and H2.\n\nmajor: Request owns the body before acquisition and closes it once on errors.\nTestRequestAcquisitionFailureClosesBody checks route exhaustion and cancellation during\ndial, the close count and an io.Pipe upload producer unblocked by the actual body Close.\n\nmajor: Close signals session cancellation before waiting on lifecycle serialization.\nTestCloseCancelsAndJoinsStartingProbes verifies prompt cancellation/join and no Running\npublication. The existing concurrent Restart/Close stress accepts cancellation as a\nvalid outcome and asserts the final closed state.\n\nmajor: access feedback distinguishes SDK attempt deadline from caller/session cancellation.\nTestAttemptTimeoutCountsAccessFailureButCallerCancelDoesNot isolates an endpoint after\nthree SDK timeouts and checks that caller cancellation does not penalize it.\n\nminor: verified TLS metadata is retained on pooled connections and assigned to H1/H2\nresponses. TestHTTPSResponseMetadataAndPoolOverflow checks verified chains and SNI.\n\nAll eight findings were addressed by the worker. The previous uncommitted review is\nhistorical evidence, not a registered formal round. The space Assistant confirmed the\nformal first round reviewed 24ed87f in t5d and found four additional major issues.\nThose were fixed in ca5de67. The additional authorized final round in t5g has\nconfirmed the four fixes with no blocking findings in the narrowed scope.\nBoth formal reports are included separately. This worker report replaces neither."
